{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_115","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > archive/yang-python/1792189000000-compiler-engineer-c4-i1.codex.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# C4 I1 — pure linked-prelude installation\n\nWorktree: \"'`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-c4-i6`; branch `c4-i1`, based on\n`origin/master` at `1fe7ddee`. The branch already had that exact name and base\nwhen this task started. No other worktree was used. Changes remain unstaged\nand uncommitted; existing untracked `collab/` files were preserved.\n\nThis completes the earlier I1-era report in\n`1791539186673-compiler-engineer-c4-i1.glm-5-3.findings.md` against landed\nI5/I6 and `ce76c846`. The earlier report'\"'s hoisted guest-import delivery is\nsuperseded by landed I4-a: guest delivery stays at the executed import\nstatement, with concrete manifest pins. The existing base module emitter,\n\"'`py/init!`, module objects and lazy body instantiation are retained.\n\n## Change\n\nThe linked hook module declared its pinned `py` dependency but never required\nit during installation. The ordinary entry wrapper'\"'s explicit \"'`require py`\nhid this gap. Requiring `pysp` alone therefore installed hook definitions\nwithout delivering the base module they reference.\n\n`yang.python.antlr.safepoint/module-uast` now requires `py` as its final\noperand, after defining its closures and immutable state placeholders, before\nthe install application returns. This order matters: a sibling read inside\na lambda is discharged only when its unconditional definition precedes every\napplication site, including `require`. No initialization runs in the child.\nThe pinned dependency is delivered through the normal linker protocol; there\nis no change to receiver admission or sender-admission stripping from\n`ce76c846`.\n\nNew runtime regressions cover all three vector VMs:\n\n- Repeated `py/init!` preserves the entire allocated heap.\n- A `sys.modules` mutation in one consuming task is absent in another task\n  consuming the same published code.\n- Standalone `require pysp` delivers both modules with an empty heap and all\n  base and hook runtime slots still `:py/uninit`, without a signal stream.\n- Installing hooks after base initialization preserves the consuming task'\"'s\n  builtin class identity and \"'`sys.modules` mutation.\n\nThe bundled profile stays selectable. Guest module bodies and statement-time\nimport delivery are unchanged.\n\n## Mechanical address regeneration\n\n`target/c4-i1-remint.clj` follows the I6 pins-round process: rebuild the\nfloat test'\"'s source packet through \"'`projected`, derive A-prime with\n`derive-envelope`, project both bundled preludes, and regenerate the\nmanifest through `publish-module!`. It checks successful links in semantic,\nstack and register formats before replacing the linked-hook manifest pin.\nRun:\n\n```sh\nclojure -Sdeps '\"'{:aliases {:i1-remint {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]}}}' \\\\\n  -M:i1-remint target/c4-i1-remint.clj\n\"'```\n\nThe generated `pysp` manifest is\n`:segment/blake3-cf017bd4063d8888c12ad6f967d49534c464d6bdcce453cb2f0a4139ea377184`.\nThe base manifest remains\n`:segment/blake3-1fa7f8fc13f58096d98412e5f5a307d5d25976c33e4d83cdc60c62b64d2b209f`.\nAll five float-address goldens and the bundled hook root mechanically\nreproduced their existing addresses. Consequently `float_address_test.cljc`\nhas no diff. No float literals or numeric rows were introduced. Publication\nrebuilds the linked hook tree, derived images, checksums and manifest.\n\n## Validation\n\n- ANTLR generation and Node REPL build completed.\n- JVM full `yang.python.antlr.linked-safepoint-test`, slow bodies enabled:\n  **15 tests, 110 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\nAdditional validation results are recorded below as the serialized lanes finish.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
